   "notes": "Published Fei et al. (2007) cold branch with the common Table 1 Ne MGD thermal parameters and Eq. 3 printed variable-exponent theta law, relative to 300 K. V0=88.967 A^3 is the fixed four-atom conventional fcc-cell volume for both branches; K0 and K0-prime remain specific to the cold equation. V0, theta0 and gamma0 are adopted source parameters; q=0.6(3) is retained with unspecified confidence/covariance. The room-temperature fit combined Finger (1981), Hemley (1989, recalculated to Dewaele 2004 ruby) and new Fei Pt/Au observations. All 14 Finger and 21 Hemley table rows, 13 separable new 300 K markers and six new 1000 K Pt-scale markers are bundled. Complete new rows, paired calibrant volumes and original weights are unrecovered. The 2000 K curve is a calculated extrapolation. See docs/literature-reproductions/fei-2007-neon.md; diagnostics do not replace published coefficients. Reported overall range is about 4.7-115 GPa; digitized/table recalculated endpoints carry their own rounding and can extend slightly above 115 GPa.",
